# EAS uploads a tarball of the whole repository to its build servers, and
# this file REPLACES .gitignore for that upload — anything not listed here
# gets sent, including what .gitignore would have kept out. That is why the
# secrets block below exists and must not be trimmed.
#
# Paths are anchored with a leading slash so they resolve at the repository
# root. pjl-field's own files are never matched.

# --- Secrets and customer data. Never upload. -------------------------
# server/data holds real leads and the hashed admin password; .env holds
# the Gmail and Twilio credentials. The root .gitignore keeps both out of
# git, and that protection does not carry over to this file.
/server/
.env
.env.*
memory/
.claude/
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.jks
*.mobileprovision
*.pem

# --- The website. ~790MB, none of it needed to build the app. ---------
# The app itself is under 1MB; without these the archive was 789MB and
# took 79 seconds just to compress.
/.git/
/.github/
/images/
/scripts/
/worker/
/docs/
/_design/
/_partials/
/*.mp4
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# --- Standard Expo and node ignores, copied from .gitignore ------------
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
/ios
/android
